# view: page
INCLUDE world.ink

=== start ===
# checkpoint: start
Somewhere close, a bucket is coming up a well on a creaking rope. It takes you a long while to work out that it's the first sound in days that isn't an engine or the wind. # place: Bowl
You're lying on a bench under a roof of woven reeds, with your cheek against wood worn smooth by a lot of hands. Past the shade run canals. Real ones, full of slow brown water. Past them the terraces climb, so green after all that dust that it hurts to look. For a moment it feels like a dream, with too much water in it to be real.
+ [Sit up.]
  ~ intro_step = "done"
  The world tilts, thinks about it, and settles. Your pickup stands parked crooked at the edge of the yard with its hood propped open, and a tow chain that isn't yours hangs coiled off the bumper.
  The bed's empty. Somebody went through the engine bay in a hurry and left the bolts lying where they fell. Whoever dragged you here didn't stick around to be thanked.
  -> hattie

=== hattie ===
A broad woman with flour on her forearms sets a cup of water on the bench beside you. Then she sits down at the other end of it, like she's got all afternoon and means to spend some of it on you. # page
Drink it slow, now. Fellow towed you in at first light, set you on my bench and drove off before I could get a word out of him. Didn't leave a name, and I didn't hear one. # speaker: Hattie
She looks over at the open hood and shakes her head, the way people do at weather.
The yard by the gate will sell you whatever they took, if you've got the coin for it. You won't get far in that truck the way it is, and you won't get far in yourself either until you've had something to eat. # speaker: Hattie
+ [Drink.]
  The water is cold and tastes of canal stone, and you drink it so fast it hurts your teeth. A bowl of hot grain follows without being asked for, and then another cup. Funny. Water never tasted this good back when there was plenty of it.
  -> END
